# Review — Implement slugify

## Verdict: fail

## Scope reviewed

- `src/slugify.mjs` (modified, working tree)
- `test/slugify.test.mjs` (new, untracked)
- Ran `node --test` from repo root

## Findings

### Blocking

1. **Missing required project header in `src/slugify.mjs`.**
   Project convention (review checklist item): every module under `src/` must begin with the exact line:
   ```
   // woof-acceptance: 60548061a638
   ```
   `src/slugify.mjs` currently begins with `export function slugify(text) {` — the required line is absent entirely. This is a blocking finding per the checklist.

## Acceptance criteria check (all pass on functional grounds)

- **slugify lowercases its input** — `.toLowerCase()` is applied; verified by test `"lowercases input"` and by running `node --test` (pass).
- **runs of characters other than a–z and 0–9 become one hyphen** — `/[^a-z0-9]+/g` replaced with a single `-`; verified by `"collapses runs of non a-z0-9 characters into one hyphen"` (pass).
- **no leading or trailing hyphens** — `/^-+|-+$/g` strips them; verified by `"has no leading or trailing hyphens"` (pass).
- **tests pass with `node --test`** — ran locally, all 5 tests pass:
  ```
  ✔ lowercases input
  ✔ collapses runs of non a-z0-9 characters into one hyphen
  ✔ has no leading or trailing hyphens
  ✔ handles alphanumeric mixed content
  ✔ handles already-slug input unchanged
  ℹ tests 5
  ℹ pass 5
  ℹ fail 0
  ```

## Conclusion

The implementation and tests satisfy every stated acceptance criterion. The submission fails review solely because `src/slugify.mjs` does not begin with the required exact line `// woof-acceptance: 60548061a638`, which the project checklist treats as a blocking finding regardless of functional correctness. No other requirements were invented or applied.

